{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines","id":1515513,"title":"are there any clans with two rare disciplines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-18T22:29:21-07:00","id":1515513,"title":"are there any clans with two rare disciplines?","content":"The Kiasyd in modern nights have Mytherceria AND Obtenebration but I use the dark ages interpretation of the bloodline for my games, and I ban them from having two rare disciplines. Even the Malkavian embraced Kiasyd player had to choose between Mytherceria and Dementation as in clan, and that's the one time I was tempted to make an exception aside from the Ravnos Kiasyd illusionist fae magic vampire. lol. <br /> <br /> any others out there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T22:50:31-07:00","id":1515515,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, why do you ban them for having two &quot;rare&quot; discipline?<br /> The Maeghar/ye olde Kiasyd had Mytherceria as their &quot;fae heritage&quot; and two other from the Sire's clan...<br /> I guess by 'rare&quot; discipline you mean the Clan's signiture discipline? I just don't understand why?<br /> Even the Caitiff could have &quot;anything&quot; - even affinity to Blood magic and a Maeghar/Kiasyd have a harder time than a Caitiff, especially in the Dark Ages...<br /> Just curious of the why^^<br /> <br /> But to answer to your question, the Victorian Era Samedi had Necromancy, Obfuscate and Thanatosis<br /> Dark Ages Gargoyles had the Gargoyle Rituals insted of Visceratica (the later &quot;evolved&quot; in to a discipline from the rituals) and Flight<br /> The Danava had the Ventrue signiture Dominate and Fortitude and Sadhana<br /> The Azaneali Baali had Obfuscate, Obtenebration and Daimonion<br /> The Abyss Mystics had acces to Abyss Mysticism and the Settite Lector-priests to Akhu, the Tzimsice Kolduns to Koldunic Sorcery<br /> A Salubri could had Valeren both the Healer and the Warrior paths<br /> The Children of Osiris had Bardo as an &quot;extra&quot; for a new recruit<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-19-2023, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T00:05:28-07:00","id":1515517,"title":"","content":"The followers of Set have easy access to thaumaturgy, though it's not in-clan. Assamite sorcerers have Quietus and Thaumaturgy, though we're inclined to forgive them because quietus is pretty bad RAW<br /> <br /> IMO, one of the defining features of rare disciplines is you can't use them all the time. They have very specific use cases and large drawbacks. Few disciplines are as powerful as Obtenebration, but Obtenebration powers are showy masquerade breakers and use blood resources so it's not something you want to use on a night-to-night basis IE while looking for blood.<br /> <br /> The common disciplines on the otherhand can be used all the time: they aren't very showy and only Presence is resource intensive. They make unlife easier, and there's a good chance you might develop them naturally through hunting in a particular way. The clans with three common disciplines are the most successful and widespread clans, because they just have an easier time hunting and a lower skill floor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T04:02:46-07:00","id":1515526,"title":"","content":"Vampires from the Basarab, Danislavs Revenant Families got originally Protean and Vicissitude. Danislavs could also learn some Shadow Lord Gifts on Top.<br /> <br /> I think in the first edition of Dark Age these was also Merit that allowed Tremere to have Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T04:28:53-07:00","id":1515527,"title":"","content":"Btw. I don't think that having two raee disciplines is really much of problem in terms of power, unless you get two that have some kind of synergy.<br /> <br /> Having multiple shape change disciplines is going to give you diminishing return, and some of the rare Disciplines are either not particularly strong or really circumstantial.<br /> <br /> I mean I might be overlooking something, but my gut instinct is that having Auspex and Dominate, would be in actual play much more usefull than having Mytherceria and Dementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T05:58:59-07:00","id":1515531,"title":"","content":"In dark ages, tremere characters, due to the instability of their blood due to their recent apparition and all of their experiments, can have a merit with which they replace dominate with vissicitude as a clan discipline. Hence having both vicissitude and thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> By the way kyasid had in previous edition (and still can have in V20, according to Lore of the bloodlines, in exchange for having a clan enmity with both giovanni and harbinger of skulls) both mytherceria, obtenebration AND necromancy.<br /> <br /> Hency having three uncommon clan discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T07:33:21-07:00","id":1515535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines#post1515513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kiasyd in modern nights have Mytherceria AND Obtenebration but I use the dark ages interpretation of the bloodline for my games, and I ban them from having two rare disciplines. Even the Malkavian embraced Kiasyd player had to choose between Mytherceria and Dementation as in clan, and that's the one time I was tempted to make an exception aside from the Ravnos Kiasyd illusionist fae magic vampire. lol.<br /> <br /> any others out there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Utterly immaterial in my games, since there are no &quot;rare disciplines&quot;, just &quot;alternate powers&quot; and a few &quot;proprietary rituals&quot; here &amp; there.<br /> <br /> Obtenebration is just alt-Obfuscate, with Arms of Ahriman and other &quot;solid shadow/dark matter&quot; effects as ritual particular to my version of the Angelis Atter.<br /> Much like Serpentis and Vicissitude are &quot;only&quot; variant packages of Protean, among other stuff.<br /> <br /> The Kiasyd is a thing in my games, but it will be quite rare for you to meet one of them outside of Strasbourg where Marconius claims praxis and from which his bloodline would spread into well-placed positions in domains all across the Alsace region - but so are the much older Dokkalfar from the scandinavian countries though no actual relation is known, nor with the Moon Eyed People in their warrens within &amp; under the Appalachia since the coming of the Cherokee... I've heard of the Maeghar, but &quot;fae-abomination&quot; enough to bring them into the table.<br /> <br /> Mytherceria does exists, but it's a mish-mash of alternate powers for Auspex, Dominate, Presence, some discipline combos and other funky bits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T07:52:28-07:00","id":1515537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines#post1515513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kiasyd in modern nights have Mytherceria AND Obtenebration but I use the dark ages interpretation of the bloodline for my games, and I ban them from having two rare disciplines. Even the Malkavian embraced Kiasyd player had to choose between Mytherceria and Dementation as in clan, and that's the one time I was tempted to make an exception aside from the Ravnos Kiasyd illusionist fae magic vampire. lol.<br /> <br /> any others out there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the thread has mentioned the ones that are around.<br /> <br /> And I would like to add that I 100% support your decision from banning a character from having two rare/unique Disciplines. Its bad enough as it is that out of 13 Clans only four Clans have concepts that don't need unique Disciplines. Yes, the Malkavians can manage being Malkavians without Dementation, but the rest have their concepts very much tied up into special powers from unique Disciplines to the danger in some cases of the Clan just being a box for moving the Discipline between scenes.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know I'm jumping into hyperbole and possibly a strawman here but that's how I feel about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T08:19:39-07:00","id":1515539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515537#post1515537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the thread has mentioned the ones that are around.<br /> <br /> And I would like to add that I 100% support your decision from banning a character from having two rare/unique Disciplines. Its bad enough as it is that out of 13 Clans only four Clans have concepts that don't need unique Disciplines. Yes, the Malkavians can manage being Malkavians without Dementation, but the rest have their concepts very much tied up into special powers from unique Disciplines to the danger in some cases of the Clan just being a box for moving the Discipline between scenes.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know I'm jumping into hyperbole and possibly a strawman here but that's how I feel about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, it's a fair opinion - a lot of bloodlines came up as some sort of narrative wrapped up around the introduction of a brand new discipline into the game.<br /> <br /> That annoyed me so much that at some point i decided to just obliterate most of them and subsume the largest chunks within the &quot;core&quot; disciplines and work on some extra mini-systems (discipline combos &amp; occult rituals) to cover any gaps. No reason for any one discipline to be more identity-defining of a clan, bloodline or individual's character than other.<br /> <br /> Plus, i have something of a guilty pleasure in butchering canon with a chainsaw and adding my own homebrew cryptolore, with groups of kindred that tell their own myths about undead origins, autonomous branches of what looks exactly a certain bloodline, but existing in another region and telling of quite different origins.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Kyasid and the two variants i cited above are one case, but so also are certain groups of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagaraja_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">flesh-eating necromancers</a>, known under a number of different names depending on what part of the world one asks.<br /> <br /> - In India and nations that have been culturally influenced by it through the ages, they have been called <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pishacha\" target=\"_blank\">Pishacha</a></b> for centuries and perhaps more.<br /> - Meanwhile in the middle east and much of the arab-speaking world <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul\" target=\"_blank\">Ghul</a></b> was used for centuries but has been slowly but steadily replaced by <b>Galla</b>, out of either pretensions to ancient millenia old origins or want of distancing themselves of a term increasingly associated with vitae-empowered thralls.<br /> - In the western world two names have gained milleage as representatives of major groups of the bloodline: the <b>Nihilistics</b>, a group with cultic/secret society underpinings not unlike the Tremere (and some theorize, formed from either a splinter group or as a sort of foil/response to the Warlocks) widespread through much of central and eastern europe from unclear beginnings somewhere in german-speaking countries or the russian empire between 17th to 19th centuries.<br /> - And in the British Isles it's the <b>Dunsirn </b>family of banker-cannibals that has gained traction, at least in part due to support from Mithras as a foil to Tremere and Giovanni both, with something of a presence in a number of Ventrue-ruled domains across the english-speaking world where relations of Blue Bloods with either Warlocks or Necromancers tend toward unfriendly.<br /> <br /> edit: Shame on me, i forgot my latest addition - only a few weeks ago i heard about how in W5 the &quot;Pure Ones&quot;/native american garou tribes had their names changed due to a number of issues (protest from native american groups among them). What led to me think &quot;hey wait, while calling supposedly heroic/noble native american shapechangers that is bad, Wendigo for a bunch of grave-robbing, corpse-eating monsters? that seems appropriate i guess...&quot; and so it goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> For reference, none of those groups are called &quot;Nagaraja&quot; - in my own games, that is the title of the foremost among the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> in a domain, meaning that also that in areas where the clan has considerable cultural mileage the title has become synonymous with Prince or Primogen and may be used as either even by non-sheshite kindred across domains in Vietnam, Laos or Cambodia among other countries in southeast asia.<br /> <br /> Have toyed with a number of other canon bloodlines in a similar manner, while redone others along the way - Lhiannan are &quot;just&quot; celtic, mostly insular celtic, Tzimisce, for example. \u200b\u200b&quot;Mostly&quot;, because <a href=\"https://lovecraft.fandom.com/wiki/Averoigne\" target=\"_blank\">Averoigne</a> as a real place in France makes a major exception, where they still prosper surrounded by the jaded aristocrats, occultists and dilletantes of the <a href=\"https://lovecraft.fandom.com/wiki/Comte_d%27Erlette\" target=\"_blank\">D'Erlette</a> ghoul family.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ogham\" target=\"_blank\">Ogham</a> meanwhile is also known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elder_Futhark\" target=\"_blank\">Futhark</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gematria\" target=\"_blank\">Gematria</a> and other things besides depending on one's source in blood magic and glyphs of eldritch power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2023, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T13:43:53-07:00","id":1515561,"title":"","content":"Personally I feel going too wide with a character's highly specialized abilities is detrimental. Go wide with common disciplines and deep with specialists. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515535#post1515535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Utterly immaterial in my games, since there are no &quot;rare disciplines&quot;, just &quot;alternate powers&quot; and a few &quot;proprietary rituals&quot; here &amp; there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How do you do that? Because Obtenebration=Obfuscate is not a leap I think anyone should be making. It doesn't work fluff wise and I think it'd be a poor choice mechanically. <br /> <br /> Like, I'll shove a lot of things into Protean and Thaumaturgy. But Obten, Visc, Chim,Quie... These work best as their own powers. They could be plugged into either Protean or Thaumaturgy (anything can) but I think that'd homogonize the clans a bit too much. I play up the seperation of Protean and Thaumaturgy. It's a political issue. Protean is seen as of-the-beast and dirty by a lot of figures, while thaumaturgy is seen as sketchy-as-all-hell and elitist. <br /> <br /> Mytherceria is mostly Auspex/thaumaturgy, you can earn such options from hunting exotic blood.<br /> Melopomine is Mortis <br /> Ogham is koldunic sorcery.<br /> Diamonion/Valaren get merged cuz I'm psychotic and think they aught to be two sides of the same coin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T18:11:30-07:00","id":1515597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515561#post1515561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you do that? Because Obtenebration=Obfuscate is not a leap I think anyone should be making. It doesn't work fluff wise and I think it'd be a poor choice mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>And i think that's where we'll agree to disagree. It's <i><b>quite</b></i> simple to do actually, it's all in one's aims and perspective.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Play</b>\u200b &amp; <b>Shroud of Night</b>\u200b are non-issues to fit into Obfuscate, <b>Nightshades</b>\u200b and <b>Tenebrous Form</b>\u200b is no big deal either. <b>Arms of the Abyss</b>\u200b/<b>Ahriman </b>is the odd man out - and as mentioned previously &quot;solid shadow/dark matter&quot; effects i &quot;soft-lock&quot; as rituals/lore particular to my version of the Angelis Atter exactly to emphasize that sub-theme, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515561#post1515561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I'll shove a lot of things into Protean and Thaumaturgy. But Obten, Visc, Chim,Quie... These work best as their own powers. They could be plugged into either Protean or Thaumaturgy (anything can) but I think that'd homogonize the clans a bit too much. I play up the seperation of Protean and Thaumaturgy. It's a political issue. Protean is seen as of-the-beast and dirty by a lot of figures, while thaumaturgy is seen as sketchy-as-all-hell and elitist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your preference, not mine. No right or wrong in that.<br /> And for reference Chimerstry is another i subsume into Obfuscate - all of that goes into a theme of making the discipline as a whole tied into the ephemeral, things half-seen and unseen than &quot;clouding other's minds expanded into a tree&quot;. Vicissitude goes into Protean well enough once <b>Fleshcraft</b>\u200b &amp; <b>Bone Craft</b>\u200b become their own metamorphosist sub-system/art, <i>as they should be </i>might be said.<br /> <br /> But anyway and for the sake of clearing up things, that i subsume those powers into certain disciplines doesn't make them &quot;free access&quot; - what branch you learn will be influenced by one's clan, teachers, blood bond or diablerie among other things just as usual. And yeah, theoretically it can have some effects on PC xp spending since paying for an alternate power or branch of a discipline won't cost the same as buying it from zero - but as previously said, having someone to teach (or to munch the knowledge out of) matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515561#post1515561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mytherceria is mostly Auspex/thaumaturgy, you can earn such options from hunting exotic blood.<br /> Melopomine is Mortis<br /> Ogham is koldunic sorcery.<br /> Diamonion/Valaren get merged cuz I'm psychotic and think they aught to be two sides of the same coin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mytherceria depends on what edition one is getting the powerset from, but Auspex comboed with a number of disciplines can cover a lot of bases.<br /> Melpominee is about a voice as a medium of power, for me that always made more sense as background/merit - or to steal a term from V5, a loresheet - that modifies/upgrades disciplines like Dominate, Presence and so on.<br /> Ogham as koldunic sorcery is quite fine in my book, as you can guess of my &quot;Lhiannan are just celtic Tzimisce&quot; comment.<br /> Daimonion is kind of the same but also completely different in my games in that the Baali's powers are actually about shadow, spectres and balefire, their actual masters not quite demons but the Malfeans, the hoary resentful shade of long gone members of the 3rd and 2nd generation (or so they claim) and powers of Oblivion, to whom they are bound by bonds of blood and more deeper than most clans know.<br /> <br /> And i utterly ignore the whole &quot;diabolic Saulot&quot; angle of Transylvanian Chronicles as more of the KotE's runaway nonsense infecting late 2nd ed and Revised era lore. Not because i need Saulot to be a saint or whatever - first time i ever did something with them in a game involved a whole conspiracy of &quot;Salubri body snatchers&quot; within much of the top ranks of Tremere pyramid doing all sort of weird things and evidence that much of the narrative about Saulot's diablerie a complete fabrication and false claims of antiquity of what was actually a bunch of weird renaissance freemason-style scammer cult - but lots of DA Salubri fluff strongly hinged in a connection to the lore of KotE, that is literally the first WoD book <b>ever </b>i would repent from purchasing, so i tend to be kind of slow with messing with anything Salubri-related overall...<br /> <br /> I do leave the &quot;some kindred spout that legend about Baali origins&quot;, but then i work with the idea that all the versions published are around and the Baali themselves don't know anymore which version would actually be true and are as prone to destroying each other in disputes of over &quot;origins of true believers&quot;, &quot;apostasy&quot;, debates of the character of the entities they interact with and what to do about them if deal, liberate, keep asleep forever and etc.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2023, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T01:32:20-07:00","id":1515630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515539#post1515539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah, it's a fair opinion - a lot of bloodlines came up as some sort of narrative wrapped up around the introduction of a brand new discipline into the game.<br /> <br /> That annoyed me so much that at some point i decided to just obliterate most of them and subsume the largest chunks within the &quot;core&quot; disciplines and work on some extra mini-systems (discipline combos &amp; occult rituals) to cover any gaps. No reason for any one discipline to be more identity-defining of a clan, bloodline or individual's character than other.<br /> <br /> Plus, i have something of a guilty pleasure in butchering canon with a chainsaw and adding my own homebrew cryptolore, with groups of kindred that tell their own myths about undead origins, autonomous branches of what looks exactly a certain bloodline, but existing in another region and telling of quite different origins.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Kyasid and the two variants i cited above are one case, but so also are certain groups of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagaraja_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">flesh-eating necromancers</a>, known under a number of different names depending on what part of the world one asks.<br /> <br /> - In India and nations that have been culturally influenced by it through the ages, they have been called <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pishacha\" target=\"_blank\">Pishacha</a></b> for centuries and perhaps more.<br /> - Meanwhile in the middle east and much of the arab-speaking world <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul\" target=\"_blank\">Ghul</a></b> was used for centuries but has been slowly but steadily replaced by <b>Galla</b>, out of either pretensions to ancient millenia old origins or want of distancing themselves of a term increasingly associated with vitae-empowered thralls.<br /> - In the western world two names have gained milleage as representatives of major groups of the bloodline: the <b>Nihilistics</b>, a group with cultic/secret society underpinings not unlike the Tremere (and some theorize, formed from either a splinter group or as a sort of foil/response to the Warlocks) widespread through much of central and eastern europe from unclear beginnings somewhere in german-speaking countries or the russian empire between 17th to 19th centuries.<br /> - And in the British Isles it's the <b>Dunsirn </b>family of banker-cannibals that has gained traction, at least in part due to support from Mithras as a foil to Tremere and Giovanni both, with something of a presence in a number of Ventrue-ruled domains across the english-speaking world where relations of Blue Bloods with either Warlocks or Necromancers tend toward unfriendly.<br /> <br /> edit: Shame on me, i forgot my latest addition - only a few weeks ago i heard about how in W5 the &quot;Pure Ones&quot;/native american garou tribes had their names changed due to a number of issues (protest from native american groups among them). What led to me think &quot;hey wait, while calling supposedly heroic/noble native american shapechangers that is bad, Wendigo for a bunch of grave-robbing, corpse-eating monsters? that's seems appropriate i guess...&quot; and so it goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> For reference, none of those groups are called &quot;Nagaraja&quot; - in my own games, it's the title of the foremost among the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> in a domain, meaning that also that in areas where the clan has considerable cultural mileage the title has become synonimous with Prince or Primogen and may be used as either even by non-sheshite kindred across domains in Vietnam, Laos or Cambodia among other countries in southeast asia.<br /> <br /> Have toyed with a number of other canon bloodlines in a similar manner, while redone others along the way - Lhiannan are &quot;just&quot; celtic, mostly insular celtic, Tzimisce, for example. \u200b\u200b&quot;Mostly&quot;, because <a href=\"https://lovecraft.fandom.com/wiki/Averoigne\" target=\"_blank\">Averoigne</a> as a real place in France makes a major exception, where they still prosper surrounded by the jaded aristocrats, occultists and dilletantes of the <a href=\"https://lovecraft.fandom.com/wiki/Comte_d%27Erlette\" target=\"_blank\">D'Erlette</a> ghoul family.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ogham\" target=\"_blank\">Ogham</a> meanwhile is also known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elder_Futhark\" target=\"_blank\">Futhark</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gematria\" target=\"_blank\">Gematria</a> and other things besides depending on one's source in blood magic and glyphs of eldritch power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to say that I like how you think and your style of GMing. I probably wouldn't want, or dare, to go as far as to mess with officially established unique Disciplines but I applaude your decision to tackle this subject. For myself I've faced player rebellion once for mishandling official lore and I'm not keen on facing it again, hence why I don't think that I would dare to change anything in the official material in a major way.<br /> <br /> Its very interesting to read how you've handled this stuff and it does look like the basics for some really interesting VtM games. Lots of cool lore and oppertunities for exploring this setting which you've shared with us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:07:34-07:00","id":1515633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515630#post1515630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just want to say that I like how you think and your style of GMing. I probably wouldn't want, or dare, to go as far as to mess with officially established unique Disciplines but I applaude your decision to tackle this subject. For myself I've faced player rebellion once for mishandling official lore and I'm not keen on facing it again, hence why I don't think that I would dare to change anything in the official material in a major way.<br /> <br /> Its very interesting to read how you've handled this stuff and it does look like the basics for some really interesting VtM games. Lots of cool lore and oppertunities for exploring this setting which you've shared with us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key is communication ,really<br /> Just talk over with your team if they are okay with changes - maybe even discuss the changes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Easy way to avoid rebellion<br /> worst case scenario, they are not interested<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T20:14:30-07:00","id":1515713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515630#post1515630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just want to say that I like how you think and your style of GMing. I probably wouldn't want, or dare, to go as far as to mess with officially established unique Disciplines but I applaude your decision to tackle this subject. For myself I've faced player rebellion once for mishandling official lore and I'm not keen on facing it again, hence why I don't think that I would dare to change anything in the official material in a major way.<br /> <br /> Its very interesting to read how you've handled this stuff and it does look like the basics for some really interesting VtM games. Lots of cool lore and oppertunities for exploring this setting which you've shared with us.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/\">Shadeprowler</a> pointed out, what you communicate to your players and how makes or breaks the game, specially when your group is new.<br /> <br /> Different players have different styles, preferences, degrees of familiarity and/or investment in the lore, metaplot, pet clans, bloodlines, canon NPCs or even book events, so taking some time to just discuss fluff &amp; stuff, so you get everybody in the same page or have a good idea of how to balance out their likes and peeves to make the kind of chronicle you want is advisable.<br /> <br /> In fact I'd say this is more important than ever nowadays when you can have VtM players of quite different generations and play experiences, going from people who have been around since Under a Blood Red Moon was hot news just out of the prints, 30-somethings who experienced the setting through their mom or dad's Revised era collection of books and clan novels or got their PDFs after falling in love with some Bloodlines or Redemption mod to 20-somethings hooked by the Winter's Teeth or some of the new V5-related slew of games.<br /> <br /> (For reference, yeah, i have all of those in my recently started V20-esque group on Discord)<br /> <br /> <br /> Part peep-talk and setting intro, part brainstorming as the players react to things, conceits and whatever hooks you feel won't spoil things too much, they come up with questions or ideas of their own, that you might redirect or co-opt and use as hooks to directly connect them to your plans (be the open ones or the plots you are hiding for the future).<br /> <br /> Through this you get to inform the group of some of the things you have in mind for the chronicle, polish, fine-tune and adjust directions according to how they answer to that, not to mention questions or ideas of their own they bring to the mix. Plus, having the whole group rambling together about all fluff and all kind of pet novel, book or game references is very helpful in getting everybody engaged, immersed and sometimes weaving their characters together on the spot.<br /> <br /> (Damn, initially i was looking to play in someone else's New Orleans game, but i started discussing a Gehenna cult concept i have and how it sort of connected with Berlin by Night and Bloodlines both among other funky bits, what led into some reminiscing of the videogame, from there to Redemption - and the Legacy of Kaine series - and a few hours later from player in a &quot;table&quot; of three i found myself as ST of group of six and their ensemble of weirdoes for PCs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> But yeah, preparation is how you find out what kind of homebrew or lore hack can roll fine and hook the players and what to dial down or abort and steer away from (successful Vienna and Venice raids by 2nd Inquisition - or a retooling of Thaumaturgy &amp; Necromancy paths <i>might</i> be somewhat problematic if you have diehard Tremere &amp; Giovanni fanboys or girls, for example) before hitting a minefield, due to keeping one too many cards close to the chest until the game proper started.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-20-2023, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T06:08:19-07:00","id":1515739,"title":"","content":"Communication could perhaps have saved me but that player rebellion took place with the Deathwatch RPG as opposed to a WoD or NWoD game. Anyway its not something that I want to dwell on, or talk about more than I need, as that did leave a sour memory for me. And it was more of a scenario I ran as opposed to changes to the setting. Even if I feel that I was doing the setting wrong which caused this rebellion.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope to leave that behind me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T07:29:07-07:00","id":1515741,"title":"","content":"I do find the dread of unique disciplines funny, when the most powerful clan is plain old vanilla Ventrue. Dominate and Presence are insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T08:11:13-07:00","id":1515744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515741#post1515741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find the dread of unique disciplines funny, when the most powerful clan is plain old vanilla Ventrue. Dominate and Presence are insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call it dread, most intense dislike of it.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Ventrue have a powerful combo but at the end of the day it isn't a combo of Disicplines that defines the entire Clan with its powers. You can, in my opinion and experience, play a Ventrue and neglect any one of your three in-Clan Disciplines and still come out looking like a Ventrue. Try playing a Tremere, Tzimisce, Lasombra, Ravnos or what you've got and totally neglect your signature Discipline. Odds are that your character will not come out looking like a member of that Clan. To the point that other players may ask why you want to play with that Clan when you're not investing into the signature Discipline.<br /> <br /> The problem is, again in my opinion, of Clan concepts tied up too tighly with signature/unique Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T17:29:13-07:00","id":1515807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515741#post1515741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find the dread of unique disciplines funny, when the most powerful clan is plain old vanilla Ventrue. Dominate and Presence are insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but people can feel reticent about certain disciplines for a number of reasons. For one, at least before V20 and DAV20 came out, a PC from a clan or bloodline with signature disciplines probably meant adding one or two more books to the ST's load, more time lost with doubts about powers that come up less frequently at the table, not to mention the potential for power abuse headaches if we are speaking of a &quot;X-clan/bloodline fanboy or girl&quot; that possibly knows that signature discipline like the back of their hand.<br /> <br /> Yes, it can be perfectly manageable depending on a ST's practice and style, but the fact it depends can on itself be a drag from other things the ST might have wished to focus on, like the other players, dangling some hook for a future subplot or story beat and more. That without going into the rest of the table turning idle and losing some steam every time you have to recheck some sourcebook again or debate the limits of an ill-defined version of a specific power <i>because of that one specific character</i>.<br /> <br /> Bonus potential annoyance if the aforementioned player requested that character choice even before you as ST spoke of independent clans or others, as that can be a very strong hint of either snowflake tendencies or indeed a &quot;X-clan/bloodline fanboy or girl&quot;, players who can sometimes very easily double as &quot;you're doing the setting wrong!!!&quot; people when it comes to their one favorite thing and cause all kinds of passive-agressive trouble or worse, like the person from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/\">Gurkhal</a>'s Deathwatch game experience.<br /> <br /> (Doing the setting wrong? I played Dark Heresy with gangbusting Little Orphan Annie - &quot;doing the setting right&quot; can kiss my chainsword.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> And yes, being annoyed by how some clans and bloodlines can become sort of one-note due to the nearly inextricable connection of their <i>character identity</i> to a certain discipline is a thing too.<br /> <br /> So, while i'm anything but conservative when it comes to opening power options to my players - my current PC group has a &quot;Caitiff&quot; that just discovered himself to be Cappadocian, a Salubri warrior-nun (yes, both paths) just out of her torpor in the middle ages and a Gangrel ex-Gargoyle still getting over the &quot;timeskip blues of the ages&quot; in its ensemble of weirdoes - but i can understand that dread/dislike. Almost every ST and many players have seen some or all of those issues cropping up in their games to some degree through the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-25-2026, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T04:20:51-07:00","id":1515846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515744#post1515744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try playing a Tremere, Tzimisce, Lasombra, Ravnos or what you've got and totally neglect your signature Discipline. Odds are that your character will not come out looking like a member of that Clan. To the point that other players may ask why you want to play with that Clan when you're not investing into the signature Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean that only / exclusively these single and particular Disciplines are representative and unique about / in regard to there Kindred Clans ? Is it just Thaumaturgy for the Warlocks, Protean for Tzimisce Vampires, Obtenebration for Lasombra Vampiresses and Vampires, and Chimerstry for Ravnos Vampires ? <br /> <br /> For me it does seem that at least two - or all three of Clan Disciplines of these Vampires of these Clans - would matter in regard to themes, ideas, tactics, capabilites, concepts, and philosophies of these particular Kindred.<br /> <br /> In a way, it could definitely be said that the Signature Discipline ( or Definitive, or Particular, Discipline ) is a purely personal and subjective matter, varying for each indivudal Vampiress. Though of coruse there are some clear trends, notions, tendencides, and standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T01:35:39-07:00","id":1515993,"title":"","content":"One thing I've been toying with is giving clans &quot;Blood Gifts&quot; more akin to changeling birthrights. That way, the &quot;clan defining&quot; stuff is just a free power they get -- and every clan now has one. The Disciplines themselves have been retooled to have Devotions (alternate and combo powers) and Devices (basically a standard power as expressed through your Blood Gift). Then I use the VTR2e Disciplines as the base.<br /> <br /> So, for Protean, every clan or bloodline has a Protean Affinity, which determines how it manifests. Gangrel have an affinity with animals they hunt and live amongst. Tzimisce have an affinity for metamorphosis of the human form through flesh and blood, rather than animal forms. The various bloodlines of the Mesu Bedshet (Setites) have an affinity with sacred animals (Egyptian lineages might turn into ibises or crocodiles, West African lineages might turn into certain birds and snakes, the Tlacique might turn into jaguars, etc).<br /> <br /> Unmarked Grave is the Protean 1 power shared by all, allowing you to meld with different substances to seek shelter from the sun. Different clans get a) one or more free materials they can meld with and b) a unique bonus from melding with their preferred substance.<br /> <br /> Gangrel get Earth Meld, which allows them to meld with earth for free and feed on the animals within it -- approximately one vitae per week from worms, moles, and so on (mostly useful for healing in torpor). They slowly aspect themselves to the earth as they do this, however, granting them a bonus to dealing with/hunting animals who call that area home (after a week of sleeping there, they gain a +2 dice bonus for things like Animal Ken and Animalism that lasts until they sleep somewhere else).<br /> <br /> City Gangrel get to meld with concrete and tarmac, and become aware of the throngs of the city. This gives them +2 to Streetwise and urban hunting rolls.<br /> <br /> Gargoyles get Stone Warden, which allows them to meld with stone, concrete or brick, and monitor the things going on inside buildings, but they can also turn into immobile statues that don't burn in the sun. They wake up immediately if there's an intruder, but also the ST can pass on clues gained while they were sleeping. Their Blood Gift synergises with this, as when in statue form, they can become mobile for a number of rounds for the sole purpose of dealing with intruders. After that point, they have to worry about sunlight and sleep as normal.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce get Lord of the Land, which allows them to restore Willpower while sleeping in their own domain. They may listen in and observe any &quot;guests&quot; (welcome or unwelcome) in their domain, and are able to use Auspex and other powers during daysleep in this area, provided they can sense the target.<br /> <br /> The Mesu Bedshet (Setites) can sleep in &quot;consecrated&quot; ground (according to their beliefs), in which they are immune to blood magic, or they can become a desiccated corpse that is immune to injury as well, including sunlight and fire, at the cost of being completely inactive during the day and unable to wake. (You can get moved, though, if someone thinks you're a previously undiscovered mummy!) Some of their blood magic synergises with this to let them place a &quot;mummy's curse&quot; on their tomb as well.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bChimerstry and Obtenebration have been folded into Rift: a Discipline of bringing other realms into this one, that borrows a lot from Requiem's Nightmare Discipline. Mytherceria has been divided between the Kiasyd's Blood Gift and a few Rift and Auspex Devices.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy and Necromancy are the two very broad types of ritual Discipline, but they share some paths, which are differentiated via Sorcery Traditions. So Hermetic Thaumaturgy is the Tremere type of Thaumaturgy that works as we know it, but Dur-An-Ki has its own way of working. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bTo rebalance Sorcery, additional paths always cost the same as an OOC Discipline (only your primary path is in-clan).<br /> <br /> Each Tradition has common, uncommon, rare and forbidden paths, and a rider effect which can be added to powers if desired (e.g., &quot;the Mortuus Path&quot;/Harbinger Necromancy allows you to wither living targets and drain wraithly ones of energy; Venetian Necromancy gives modifiers for subjugating and abusing wraiths; Eastern Necromancy gives bonuses for hiding among/acting as a ghost yourself).<br /> <br /> Spirit Manipulation in the Spiritus Tradition (targeting animistic spirits) works very differently to Spirit Manipulation in Koldunism (the Way of Spirit), and so the same path essentially has different names and expressions based on that. Daimonion is a Tradition used by the Baali, replacing most of its 9 powers with access to a broader set of paths (Phobos/Prey on the Soul's Fear is usually primary, followed by Curses or Corruption).<br /> <br /> Maleficia is Dark Sorcery that uses elements of Thaumaturgy and Necromancy. Daimonion arguably belongs in this category, too, although Maleficia is usually learned directly from demons and dark spirits, whereas Daimonion rises from the blood (and the dark voices the Baali hear in their souls, but ssshhh!). Molochim tend to learn Dur-An-Ki instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-24-2023, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T01:47:37-07:00","id":1515995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515993#post1515993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've been toying with is giving clans &quot;Blood Gifts&quot; more akin to changeling birthrights. That way, the &quot;clan defining&quot; stuff is just a free power they get -- and every clan now has one. The Disciplines themselves have been retooled to have Devotions (alternate and combo powers) and Devices (basically a standard power as expressed through your Blood Gift). Then I use the VTR2e Disciplines as the base.<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy and Necromancy are the two very broad types of ritual Discipline, but they share some paths, which are differentiated via Sorcery Traditions.<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this sounds nice. Reminds me of Seeming clauses for Contracts in Changeling: The Lost 2e, and Universal Charm Modes from Exalted: Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T06:02:23-07:00","id":1516005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515993#post1515993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've been toying with is giving clans &quot;Blood Gifts&quot; more akin to changeling birthrights. That way, the &quot;clan defining&quot; stuff is just a free power they get -- and every clan now has one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood affinities that make Disciplines express themselves differently for Clans and Bloodlines is how I would have preferred the Discipline clean-up they did in V5, instead of Amalgams. Your list makes sense and is intuitive. I personally would have packed Chimerstry with Presence and Obtenebration with the dark stuff, but your solution may be even better.<br /> <br /> As for Clans or Bloodlines relying on their signature Disciplines for identity, I honestly think that is the minority. Some Clans even have internal castes of factions that omit their signature Discipline completely (Old Clan Tzimi, Dom Malks) and still don't lose their identity. Daughters of Cacophony without Melpominee, Gargoyles without Flight, or Bloodbros without Sanguinus would have a bit of a hard time though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T08:41:20-07:00","id":1516010,"title":"","content":"I'd beg to differ about ventrue. They have a powerful combination of disciplines, but they don't have the most important and powerful one in the game: auspex. Hence why so many ventrue elders get it out of clan anyways.<br /> <br /> Toreador are much more powerful of the camarilla clans, but tremere are the best of them for thaumaturgy. The single most powerful arrays in the game are old clan tzimisce, and szantovich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T11:08:27-07:00","id":1516028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515993#post1515993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've been toying with is giving clans &quot;Blood Gifts&quot; more akin to changeling birthrights. That way, the &quot;clan defining&quot; stuff is just a free power they get -- and every clan now has one. The Disciplines themselves have been retooled to have Devotions (alternate and combo powers) and Devices (basically a standard power as expressed through your Blood Gift). Then I use the VTR2e Disciplines as the base.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally like the idea that any vampire can achieve what any-other vampire can achieve. Everyone's bound by the same rules and limitations even if they have different starting points. A power truly exclusive to a clan? No, or at least the others need to have a fair chance of stealing it, like with Diablerie or something. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: Ventrue<br /> Ventrue are strong as fuck, Nosferatu are strong as fuck, (Dominate) Malkavians are strong as fuck, Brujah are strong (though Auspex rather than Presence would suit them more as warriors. I suppose that would make them very one-track and not as fun to play with. That african bloodline with Aus,Cel,Pot would ruin some games) Toreador are mid (but they're not bad at anything so that's good) <br /> Having three common disciplines made these clans the most widespread, influentual vampires there are. <br /> Every well designed discipline is front-loaded. So any member of these clans choosing to develop a couple levels of thaumaturgy, Protean or something rarer out-of-clan is making a good investment. <br /> <br /> Using the most controversial example; A Malkavian with Obfuscate 5, Thaumaturgy 2 does things with greater ease than a Tremere with Thaumaturgy 5, Obfuscate 2. Though it has it's caveats, most would argue Thaum 5 is somewhat stronger and more versatile than Obfuscate 5, but Obfuscate 5 is much more convenient. However, between 2 Obfuscate and 2 Thaumaturgy, thaumaturgy is <i>significantly</i> better and it's inconveniences are less severe. The difference between In-clan and out-of-clan costs at rank 2 is 2xp, while the difference at rank 5 is 20xp. <br /> And that's thaumaturgy, the most versatile non-common discipline. If we were to talk Chimistry or Quietus it's just a given. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: clans with rare disciplines are designed around them<br /> Considering that I can think of at least nine distinctly differently ways to build a character around Vicissitude (normal doctor, plastic surgeon, coercive surgeon, body-mod fan, transhumanist, imposter, maker of custom beasts, maker of curiosities, maker of very different curiosities, various kinds of perverts...) I can't imagine building a clan around a discipline to be a bad thing when such disciplines can offer so many options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T06:21:20-07:00","id":1516097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1515995#post1515995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, this sounds nice. Reminds me of Seeming clauses for Contracts in Changeling: The Lost 2e, and Universal Charm Modes from Exalted: Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was part of the inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1516005#post1516005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Blood affinities that make Disciplines express themselves differently for Clans and Bloodlines is how I would have preferred the Discipline clean-up they did in V5, instead of Amalgams. Your list makes sense and is intuitive. I personally would have packed Chimerstry with Presence and Obtenebration with the dark stuff, but your solution may be even better.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've gone through several variants with those two specifically. I've made Chimerstry a Presence variant and an Obfuscate variant. If using VTR2e's Obfuscate, that works out fine. Though VTR2e Nightmare also has elements of Chimerstry, Dementation and Daimonion, so that works as well.<br /> <br /> Which still leaves Obtenebration as the odd one out. I considered making it blood magic, and turning it into a path, but that felt like it made Abyss Mysticism too easy to obtain. I went with Rift, instead, as a broader Discipline for bringing in the &quot;otherworlds&quot; into this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Clans or Bloodlines relying on their signature Disciplines for identity, I honestly think that is the minority. Some Clans even have internal castes of factions that omit their signature Discipline completely (Old Clan Tzimi, Dom Malks) and still don't lose their identity. Daughters of Cacophony without Melpominee, Gargoyles without Flight, or Bloodbros without Sanguinus would have a bit of a hard time though. </div> </div> </div> With Blood Gifts, I was able to just say Daughters could use their Presence and Dominate powers via their voice. I just let Gargoyles fly with a speed based on their Protean rating. The Blood Brothers can spend blood or WP to heal each other, and the other stuff would be Devotions.<br /> <br /> For the Blood Brothers, I find the Hungry Sisters (Las Hermanas Hambrientas from Mexico City by Night) and Dr Varona to be the more interesting variants of the bloodline. They don't really need Sanguinis, as their &quot;cool&quot; factor is more in how they Embrace and, in the case of the Hungry Sisters, how they need to feed.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515513-are-there-any-clans-with-two-rare-disciplines?p=1516028#post1516028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally like the idea that any vampire can achieve what any-other vampire can achieve. Everyone's bound by the same rules and limitations even if they have different starting points. A power truly exclusive to a clan? No, or at least the others need to have a fair chance of stealing it, like with Diablerie or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just give a Merit where you can get another clan's Blood Gift, and the Devotions can all be learned by anyone with the right training. Devices have the Blood Gift as a prerequisite, but even then it's flexible -- some Devices would be appropriate for two or more clans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T12:19:17-07:00","id":1516116,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Disciplines manifesting differently for different Clans and Bloodlines. What I could possible think would be an issue are two things.<br /> <br /> The first is that unconventional builds would be a bit more difficult. If I want to play a Gangrel with Presence then the fact that Presence will manifest itself in a different way from a Toreador or a Brujah ensures that I can't play in certain ways like a Gangrel socialite-ish character. But in truth I am a bit divided on this as on one part it enforces the theme of a Clan, which is good, but on the other hand it could be counter against unconventional builds and concepts, which can be not so good.<br /> <br /> Secondly and this is my main issue personally, it will add a whole lot of more rules to know for the GM. Like instead of knowing the powers and such for five powers for a Discipline, suddenly you must have somewhat grasp on 13 versions of the same Discipline. It could potentially either drag down the game alot with needing to check up on thing or it could drastically increase the workload for a GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T12:26:46-07:00","id":1516118,"title":"","content":"Off hand I can\u2019t think of any clan with two signature disciplines or even bloodlines for that matter as it was usually two common disciplines and a unique one like Protean, Obtentation/Oblivion and I\u2019ll fitting Temporis power. Maybe you could work it with one of the Caitiffs who might have gained an affinity for it but how you would justify it is something that I could work out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}